{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting It Right", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Stick to Your Routines", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe  necessity, duty, advice, or strong disapproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Wh-Clause With Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can make sentences with wh-clauses followed by the infinitive (to + verb).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use these sentences if you want to talk about ways or methods of doing something. Often, you can use <span class=\"strong\">should</span> in these sentences as well.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'm not sure <span class=\"strong\">what</span> to do with my hair for the wedding.<br/>I'm not sure <span class=\"strong\">what</span> <span class=\"underline\">I should do</span> with my hair for the wedding.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The travel agent didn't know <span class=\"strong\">how </span>to  book the ticket online. <br/><span class=\"italic\"> The travel agent didn't know <span class=\"strong\">how</span> <span class=\"underline\">he should book</span> the ticket online. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Notice the use of the pronoun before <span class=\"strong\">should</span>, followed by the base form of the verb (no \u201cto\u201d). This pronoun refers to the same subject that is in the main clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I didn't know what to do. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Nobody told me how to organize my time. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Past Perfect Continuous for Habitual Actions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the Past Perfect Continuous (also called the Past Perfect Progressive) when you want to describe a habit that occurred repeatedly over a period of time. This verb tense tells you that these habitual actions occurred before another time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect Continuous to talk about an action that happened repeatedly before another time or activity in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Past Perfect Continuous form</span>:<br/> <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">had + been + verb -ing</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I didn't realize that I <span class=\"strong\">had been wearing</span> the same outfit to work every week until my co-worker commented on my boring sense of style.<br/><br/>  I <span class=\"strong\">had been going</span> to the gym during my lunch hour for months until my work schedule changed and I wasn't able to go anymore.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I had been spending too much time putting out fires. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had been wasting a lot of time trying to do things without proper planning.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "call to action ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a strong message to do something about a situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I read a book by this guru of time management. It was a call to action for me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about your routines.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to put out fires", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to solve immediate, urgent problems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had been spending too much time putting out fires.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the trick is", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the secret way of doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The trick is to move from doing what is urgent to what is important. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "routine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an action you do on a regular basis over a period of time (every day, every week, etc.)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Another secret is making routines that match your priorities, and sticking to them. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "required ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "necessary", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  When you plan your exercise routine, it frees up time and energy required for other things.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take action", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Planning is required to take action in other areas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le18ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Identify the ways to save time presented in this lesson then  make a list of them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, discuss other ways of saving time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online. Find 3 more ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a detailed list of suggestions to help people save time. For each suggestion, write 1 - 2 sentences giving examples.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your list to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss ways of sa